# React component structure

`src/popup/App.tsx` and `src/options/App.tsx` are already large. When touching them, **extract** focused pieces instead of growing the roots.

## Rules

- New UI sections → `src/popup/components/` or `src/options/components/` (match neighbors like `EditorPanel`, `RuleItem`, `ImportModal`).
- Reusable logic → colocated hooks; keep App as orchestration (state wiring, top-level effects).
- Never define components inside components.
- Prefer composition and clear props over passing sprawling context objects unless that pattern already exists for the feature.
- Do not drive-by rewrite unrelated App regions; extract the concern you are changing.

```tsx
// ❌ Growing App further
export function App() {
  return (
    <>
      {/* …hundreds of lines… */}
      <div className="new-feature">{/* large inline UI */}</div>
    </>
  );
}

// ✅ Extract
import { NewFeature } from './components/NewFeature';

export function App() {
  return (
    <>
      {/* … */}
      <NewFeature {...needed} />
    </>
  );
}
```

